RSLive Content — license map

This repository contains several different kinds of material. They do not all share one license.

Editorial content
-----------------

First-party editorial content in `src/content/docs/**` is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license (`CC-BY-SA-4.0`), unless a file or embedded third-party material states otherwise.

Canonical license:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Detailed RSLive attribution and scope rules:
- `LICENSE-CONTENT.md`
- `NOTICE.md`
- https://rslive.ru/license.txt

Software and repository automation
----------------------------------

First-party software code, scripts and workflows that are separately identified as software are licensed under GNU General Public License version 3 (`GPL-3.0-only`) unless stated otherwise. The complete GPLv3 text is preserved in `LICENSE-CODE`.

Data and third-party material
-----------------------------

`map-data/**`, provider snapshots, third-party media, quotations, trademarks, official documents and other externally sourced material may be subject to separate licenses, database rights, terms of use or other legal bases. Their specific provenance and notices take precedence over this repository-level summary.

Facts, ideas, public-domain material and government rules do not become proprietary merely because they are described by RSLive.

Historical note
---------------

Earlier revisions of this repository were distributed with GNU GPLv3 as the root license. Rights already granted for those copies are not revoked by the later adoption of CC BY-SA 4.0 for RSLive editorial content.
